{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_h2caaszi3ldp23tstyt6zbigjlmsn7ixlmzwcyxtlblen6aktz2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. 6+6+8+19+33 = **72 tests**, all passing, with every artifact row checked off.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe C library (`c_src/src/lib.c`, one translation unit, 11 exported functions) was verified against `src/lib.rs` through a differential suite that `dlopen`s **both** `.so` files and calls only exported symbols.\n\n**Phase A — artifacts created:** `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (30 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (33 rows), plus `verify_all.sh`.\n\n**Feature combinations:** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and `CMakeLists.txt` has no options/`#ifdef`s → exactly **one** configuration. `verify_all.sh` still derives the power set mechanically so it survives future features. I additionally verified both cargo **profiles** (`dev` and `release`), since the release profile is the shipping artifact.\n\n**Two real defects found and fixed:**\n\n1. **Null-pointer behaviour diverged.** `arr == NULL` gave **SIGSEGV in C** but **SIGABRT in Rust** — written as Rust place expressions, `(*arr).count` makes rustc emit a null check under `-C debug-assertions`, turning C's silent segfault into a panic + abort. I changed `src/lib.rs` to access fields via `wrapping_byte_add` + `core::ptr::{read, write}` (as unchecked as C's `->`). All null cases now match exactly, in both profiles. I also replaced an `unwrap_unchecked` on the `operation_func` parameter with a transmute at the call site, so a NULL callback jumps to address 0 like C rather than hitting Rust UB.\n\n2. **The test harness was silently useless at first.** `cargo test` does **not** build `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` artifacts, so the suite was loading a stale `.so`. I caught this only because I mutation-tested: three deliberately broken versions of `lib.rs` all \"passed\". `rust_so_path()` now rejects any artifact older than the sources and self-builds into a private `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.\n\n**Mutation-tested for real detection power** (documented in `SYMBOLS.md`): 7 non-equivalent mutations were all caught — including two that only rare paths detect: `FOREACH`'s `!=` → `<` (caught *only* by the negative-`count` runaway test) and the null-check regression (caught *only* by the crash-parity tests). Two further mutations were confirmed *semantically equivalent* rather than missed.\n\n**Notable C quirks deliberately preserved, not \"fixed\":** the `weight = 1` (not 0) special case at index 0; `FOREACH`'s `!=` termination test; negative `count` stored verbatim by `init_result_array`; unvalidated negative indices in `compare_results_in_array`; and two's-complement wrapping at every overflow site.\n\n**One documented UB-only divergence (E30):** `modulo_operation(INT_MIN, -1)` raises **SIGFPE** in C (bare `idiv`). No return value can match a hardware trap, so Rust uses `wrapping_rem` and returns 0; the input is unreachable from `arrayfunc`. The test pins down both sides' behaviour so it can't change silently.\n\nRun everything with `./verify_all.sh --offline`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1644,"cache_read_input_tokens":174189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1644,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55fd6b2a-7b82-4260-9215-9268aa91a396","uuid":"df144676-e6f9-4eee-8fcc-b746994ae409","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:55:03.857Z"}
